@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g8-fees-nouns`
IMPORT `g8-fees-draft`
IMPORT `g8-fees-as-made`
IMPORT `g8-fees-as-amended`
IMPORT `g8-fees`

-- g8-tests-reg3.l4: regulation 3 (update of fees) and the figures it gives on a day.
--
-- THE INDEX READINGS BELOW ARE ILLUSTRATIVE.  The sources contain no reading of the consumer price index and no
-- notice of the Director General; the numbers are chosen so that the arithmetic can be done by hand, and nothing
-- in this file says what the index was.  The tests assume that a reading carries a `month of the index` one
-- month before the month it is published in; the sources do not say how long a reading takes to appear, which is
-- why regulation 3(a) is read off the PUBLICATION day of a reading and the month of the index is used by one
-- alternative reading only.
--
--   published 15.6.2025, relating to May 2025,  value 100
--   published 15.7.2025, relating to June 2025, value 100.5
--   published 15.11.2025, relating to October 2025, value 101.25
--   published 15.11.2026, relating to October 2026, value 102.515625  (= 101.25 x 1.0125)
--
-- Expected values, decided from regulation 3(a) and the printed figures BEFORE any run (work/g8/expectations.md §4):
--   first update day 1.1.2026: new index = the reading published in November 2025 = 101.25; base index = the reading
--     published in the month before the commencement (16.7.2025), June 2025 = 100;  rate of change 1.25%.
--   194 -> 196.425 -> 196.  284 -> 287.55 -> 288.  398 -> 402.975 -> 403.  40 -> 40.5, an exact half: 41 half up, 40 half to even or down.
--   second update day 1.1.2027: new = November 2026 = 102.515625; base = November 2025 = 101.25; rate again 1.25%.
--   chain (round at every update): 196 -> 198.45 -> 198; 288 -> 291.6 -> 292; 403 -> 408.0375 -> 408; 41 -> 41.5125 -> 42.
--   once at the end: 194 x 1.0125^2 = 198.88 -> 199; 284 -> 291.14 -> 291; 398 -> 408.01 -> 408; 40 -> 41.006 -> 41.
--   158 (took effect 4.5.2026): not updated on 1.1.2026; on 1.1.2027 158 x 1.0125 = 159.975 -> 160.

§ `Tests of regulation 3`

§§ `Names for the test data`

GIVETH A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
vM MEANS `the Fees Regulations as made`

GIVETH A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
vA MEANS `the Fees Regulations as amended`

GIVETH A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
vD MEANS `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations`

GIVETH A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
sPractical MEANS `the service of sitting a practical exam`

GIVETH A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
sTheory MEANS `the service of sitting a theoretical exam`

GIVETH A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
sLicence MEANS `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal`

GIVETH A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
sTemporary MEANS `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal`

GIVETH A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
sObjPractical MEANS `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam`

GIVETH A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
sObjTheory MEANS `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam`

GIVETH A `Price index reading`
`the reading published on 15 June 2025` MEANS
    `Price index reading` WITH `year of the index` IS 2025, `month of the index` IS 5, `published on` IS YMD 2025 6 15, `value of the index` IS 100

GIVETH A `Price index reading`
`the reading published on 15 July 2025` MEANS
    `Price index reading` WITH `year of the index` IS 2025, `month of the index` IS 6, `published on` IS YMD 2025 7 15, `value of the index` IS 100.5

GIVETH A `Price index reading`
`the reading published on 15 November 2025` MEANS
    `Price index reading` WITH `year of the index` IS 2025, `month of the index` IS 10, `published on` IS YMD 2025 11 15, `value of the index` IS 101.25

GIVETH A `Price index reading`
`the reading published on 15 November 2026` MEANS
    `Price index reading` WITH `year of the index` IS 2026, `month of the index` IS 10, `published on` IS YMD 2026 11 15, `value of the index` IS 102.515625

GIVETH A `Price index reading`
`a second reading published on 20 June 2025` MEANS
    `Price index reading` WITH `year of the index` IS 2025, `month of the index` IS 5, `published on` IS YMD 2025 6 20, `value of the index` IS 99

GIVETH A `Price index reading`
`a reading published on 15 June 2025 with a zero value` MEANS
    `Price index reading` WITH `year of the index` IS 2025, `month of the index` IS 5, `published on` IS YMD 2025 6 15, `value of the index` IS 0

GIVETH A LIST OF `Price index reading`
`the illustrative readings` MEANS
    LIST `the reading published on 15 June 2025`
       , `the reading published on 15 July 2025`
       , `the reading published on 15 November 2025`
       , `the reading published on 15 November 2026`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Price index reading`
`the readings without one published in June 2025` MEANS
    LIST `the reading published on 15 July 2025`
       , `the reading published on 15 November 2025`
       , `the reading published on 15 November 2026`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Price index reading`
`the readings with two published in June 2025` MEANS
    LIST `the reading published on 15 June 2025`
       , `a second reading published on 20 June 2025`
       , `the reading published on 15 July 2025`
       , `the reading published on 15 November 2025`
       , `the reading published on 15 November 2026`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Price index reading`
`the readings with a zero base` MEANS
    LIST `a reading published on 15 June 2025 with a zero value`
       , `the reading published on 15 July 2025`
       , `the reading published on 15 November 2025`
       , `the reading published on 15 November 2026`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Price index reading`
`the readings without one published in November 2026` MEANS
    LIST `the reading published on 15 June 2025`
       , `the reading published on 15 July 2025`
       , `the reading published on 15 November 2025`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Price index reading`
`the readings without one published in November 2025` MEANS
    LIST `the reading published on 15 June 2025`
       , `the reading published on 15 July 2025`
       , `the reading published on 15 November 2026`

-- The inputs under the reading the encoding takes, and under any other reading with notices.
GIVEN readings IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
GIVETH AN `Inputs of regulation 3`
taken readings MEANS
    `the inputs of regulation 3 under the reading the encoding takes, with the readings` readings

GIVEN reading IS A `Reading of regulation 3`
      readings IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
      notices IS A LIST OF `Fee update notice`
GIVETH AN `Inputs of regulation 3`
`the test inputs under the reading` reading `with the readings` readings `and the notices` notices MEANS
    `Inputs of regulation 3` WITH
        `index readings` IS readings
        `the regulations came into force on` IS `the Fees Regulations as made came into force on`
        `the reading of regulation 3` IS reading
        `notices of the Director General` IS notices

GIVEN reading IS A `Reading of regulation 3`
GIVETH AN `Inputs of regulation 3`
`the illustrative inputs under the reading` reading MEANS
    `the test inputs under the reading` reading `with the readings` `the illustrative readings` `and the notices` EMPTY

§§ `The text as made: before the first update day, the printed figure`

-- Before 1.1.2026 no update has happened and no reading is needed: even with no readings at all the printed figure is the answer.
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, under` (taken EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 194
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, under` (taken EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 194
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sObjPractical `on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, under` (taken EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sLicence `on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, under` (taken EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 284
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sTemporary `on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, under` (taken EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 398

-- Before the regulations came into force no fee was payable under them.
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2025 7 15) `, under` (taken EMPTY) EQUALS NOTHING

-- A head the text as made does not price is silent on every day.
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sTheory `on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, under` (taken EMPTY) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sObjTheory `on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, under` (taken (`the illustrative readings`)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sTheory `on the day` (YMD 2027 6 1) `, under` (taken (`the illustrative readings`)) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `The text as made: the first update day, 1 January 2026`

#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (taken (`the illustrative readings`)) EQUALS JUST 196
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sLicence `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (taken (`the illustrative readings`)) EQUALS JUST 288
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sTemporary `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (taken (`the illustrative readings`)) EQUALS JUST 403
