§§ `The draft was never in force`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the fee payable in` vD `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, under` (taken (`the illustrative readings`)) BECAUSE "the SimpLEX draft was never in force, so no fee is payable under it on any day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the fee payable in` vD `for the service` sTheory `on the day` (YMD 2030 1 1) `, under` (taken (`the illustrative readings`)) BECAUSE "the SimpLEX draft was never in force, so no fee is payable under it on any day"

§§ `Missing readings: a named refusal, in return position`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (taken EMPTY) BECAUSE "regulation 3(a) needs the index of a month, and no reading for that month was supplied"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (taken (`the readings without one published in June 2025`)) BECAUSE "regulation 3(a) needs the index of a month, and no reading for that month was supplied"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (taken (`the readings without one published in November 2025`)) BECAUSE "regulation 3(a) needs the index of a month, and no reading for that month was supplied"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, under` (taken (`the readings without one published in November 2026`)) BECAUSE "regulation 3(a) needs the index of a month, and no reading for that month was supplied"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (taken (`the readings with two published in June 2025`)) BECAUSE "regulation 3(a) speaks of the index of a month, and two or more readings for that month were supplied"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (taken (`the readings with a zero base`)) BECAUSE "regulation 3(a) divides by the base index, and the base index supplied is not a positive number"

-- A silent head stays NOTHING even when readings are missing: nothing needs updating.
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sTheory `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (taken EMPTY) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `A fall in the index: regulation 3(a) states no floor`

-- "The rate of change of the new index compared to the base index": 99 against 100 is a change of minus 1%.  The text
-- says nothing about not going below the printed figure, so the amount goes down: 194 x 0.99 = 192.06 -> 192;
-- 40 x 0.99 = 39.6 -> 40; 284 x 0.99 = 281.16 -> 281; 398 x 0.99 = 394.02 -> 394.
GIVETH A `Price index reading`
`a reading published on 15 November 2025 that is lower than the June one` MEANS
    `Price index reading` WITH `year of the index` IS 2025, `month of the index` IS 10, `published on` IS YMD 2025 11 15, `value of the index` IS 99

GIVETH A LIST OF `Price index reading`
`the readings with a fall` MEANS
    LIST `the reading published on 15 June 2025`
       , `a reading published on 15 November 2025 that is lower than the June one`

#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (taken (`the readings with a fall`)) EQUALS JUST 192
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sObjPractical `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (taken (`the readings with a fall`)) EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sLicence `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (taken (`the readings with a fall`)) EQUALS JUST 281
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sTemporary `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (taken (`the readings with a fall`)) EQUALS JUST 394

