#ASSERT `the fee under the Fees Regulations in the vintage for the service on the day` vA sTheory (YMD 2027 1 1) (`the illustrative readings`) EQUALS JUST 160
#ASSERT `the fee under the Fees Regulations in the vintage for the service on the day` vM sTheory (YMD 2026 1 1) EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the fee under the Fees Regulations in the vintage for the service on the day` vM sPractical (YMD 2025 7 15) EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT REFUSED `the fee under the Fees Regulations in the vintage for the service on the day` vM sPractical (YMD 2026 1 1) EMPTY BECAUSE "regulation 3(a) needs the index of a month, and no reading for that month was supplied"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the fee under the Fees Regulations in the vintage for the service on the day` vD sPractical (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY BECAUSE "the SimpLEX draft was never in force, so no fee is payable under it on any day"

§§ `Alternative readings of regulation 3, each callable`

-- Alternative on rounding an exact half (40 x 1.0125 = 40.5): to the even shekel, 40; down, 40; up (taken), 41.
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sObjPractical `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (`the illustrative inputs under the reading` (`the reading of regulation 3 that rounds a half shekel to the even shekel`)) EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sObjPractical `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (`the illustrative inputs under the reading` (`the reading of regulation 3 that rounds a half shekel down`)) EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sObjPractical `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (`the illustrative inputs under the reading` (`the reading of regulation 3 that the encoding takes`)) EQUALS JUST 41
-- No exact half in the other figures: every rounding gives the same figure.
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (`the illustrative inputs under the reading` (`the reading of regulation 3 that rounds a half shekel to the even shekel`)) EQUALS JUST 196
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (`the illustrative inputs under the reading` (`the reading of regulation 3 that rounds a half shekel down`)) EQUALS JUST 196

-- Alternative on when the rounding is done: once, after the last update day.  The two readings differ on 1.1.2027.
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, under` (`the illustrative inputs under the reading` (`the reading of regulation 3 that rounds once, after the last update day`)) EQUALS JUST 199
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sObjPractical `on the day` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, under` (`the illustrative inputs under the reading` (`the reading of regulation 3 that rounds once, after the last update day`)) EQUALS JUST 41
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sLicence `on the day` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, under` (`the illustrative inputs under the reading` (`the reading of regulation 3 that rounds once, after the last update day`)) EQUALS JUST 291
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sTemporary `on the day` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, under` (`the illustrative inputs under the reading` (`the reading of regulation 3 that rounds once, after the last update day`)) EQUALS JUST 408
-- On 1.1.2026 there is one update only, so the two roundings agree.
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (`the illustrative inputs under the reading` (`the reading of regulation 3 that rounds once, after the last update day`)) EQUALS JUST 196

-- Alternative on the base index of the first update day: the index RELATING to June 2025 (value 100.5), not the one published in June 2025 (value 100).
-- 194 x 101.25 / 100.5 = 195.45 -> 195;  284 -> 286.12 -> 286;  398 -> 400.97 -> 401;  40 -> 40.30 -> 40.
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (`the illustrative inputs under the reading` (`the reading of regulation 3 that takes the index relating to the month before the commencement`)) EQUALS JUST 195
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sLicence `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (`the illustrative inputs under the reading` (`the reading of regulation 3 that takes the index relating to the month before the commencement`)) EQUALS JUST 286
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sTemporary `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (`the illustrative inputs under the reading` (`the reading of regulation 3 that takes the index relating to the month before the commencement`)) EQUALS JUST 401
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sObjPractical `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (`the illustrative inputs under the reading` (`the reading of regulation 3 that takes the index relating to the month before the commencement`)) EQUALS JUST 40
-- That reading only changes the FIRST update day: from 1.1.2027 the base index is the November one in both.  The 2027 figure
-- differs only through the rounded 2026 figure it chains from (195 x 1.0125 = 197.4375 -> 197).
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, under` (`the illustrative inputs under the reading` (`the reading of regulation 3 that takes the index relating to the month before the commencement`)) EQUALS JUST 197

-- Alternative on an amount fixed later: 158 starts at the principal regulations' first update day, 1.1.2026.
-- On 4.5.2026: 158 x 1.0125 = 159.975 -> 160 (taken: 158).  On 1.1.2027: 160 x 1.0125 = 162.0 -> 162 (taken: 160).
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vA `for the service` sTheory `on the day` (YMD 2026 5 4) `, under` (`the illustrative inputs under the reading` (`the reading of regulation 3 that updates a later amount from the first update day of the regulations`)) EQUALS JUST 160
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vA `for the service` sTheory `on the day` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, under` (`the illustrative inputs under the reading` (`the reading of regulation 3 that updates a later amount from the first update day of the regulations`)) EQUALS JUST 162
-- The same reading leaves a figure of the principal regulations unchanged.
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vA `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, under` (`the illustrative inputs under the reading` (`the reading of regulation 3 that updates a later amount from the first update day of the regulations`)) EQUALS JUST 198

-- Alternative on narrowing (b): the amended objection charge is a new provision from 4.5.2026, so it starts at 1.1.2027.
#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — the amount of the stated fee` (`as amended, regulation 2(b) — the charge for an objection to the score of the theoretical exam, taken as a new provision from the day of the amendment`) `on the day` (YMD 2026 5 4) `after the updates, under` (taken (`the illustrative readings`)) EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — the amount of the stated fee` (`as amended, regulation 2(b) — the charge for an objection to the score of the theoretical exam, taken as a new provision from the day of the amendment`) `on the day` (YMD 2027 1 1) `after the updates, under` (taken (`the illustrative readings`)) EQUALS 41
-- The taken record, on the same days: 41 on 4.5.2026 and 42 on 1.1.2027.
#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — the amount of the stated fee` (`as amended, regulation 2(b) — the charge for an objection to the score of the theoretical exam`) `on the day` (YMD 2026 5 4) `after the updates, under` (taken (`the illustrative readings`)) EQUALS 41
#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — the amount of the stated fee` (`as amended, regulation 2(b) — the charge for an objection to the score of the theoretical exam`) `on the day` (YMD 2027 1 1) `after the updates, under` (taken (`the illustrative readings`)) EQUALS 42

-- Alternative on from when an update binds: the day of the Director General's notice under regulation 3(b).
GIVETH A LIST OF `Fee update notice`
`a notice of 20 February 2026 for the update of 2026` MEANS
    LIST (`Fee update notice` WITH `year of the update day` IS 2026, `published in Reshumot on` IS YMD 2026 2 20)

GIVETH A `Reading of regulation 3`
`the reading from the notice` MEANS `the reading of regulation 3 that lets an update bind from the Director General's notice`

#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vM `for the service` sPractical `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, under` (`the test inputs under the reading` (`the reading from the notice`) `with the readings` (`the illustrative readings`) `and the notices` (`a notice of 20 February 2026 for the update of 2026`)) EQUALS JUST 194
