§§ `Alternative reading: the objection charge is "an amount", not "a fee", and is not updated`

-- Regulation 2(b) says "an amount of NIS 40"; (a), (c) and (d) say "a fee of"; regulation 3(a) updates "the amounts of the
-- fees" in regulation 2.  Taken: the objection charge is updated with the rest (40 -> 41 on 1.1.2026, 42 on 1.1.2027).
-- Alternative: it stays as printed.  The other figures are not touched by the alternative.
