§§ `Open question: "these regulations" in the amended text can be the amending regulations`

-- Regulation 3(a) keys its first update day and its first base index on "the commencement day of these regulations".  The
-- inputs carry that day, so a caller who reads "these regulations" in the amended text as the amending regulations
-- (4.5.2026) can supply it.  Then 158 is first updated on 1.1.2027 against the index published in the month before
-- 4.5.2026, April 2026 (illustrative value 100): 158 x 102.515625 / 100 = 161.97 -> 162.  Taken (the principal
-- regulations' day, base November 2025 = 101.25): 158 x 1.0125 = 159.975 -> 160.
GIVETH A `Price index reading`
`the reading published on 15 April 2026` MEANS
    `Price index reading` WITH `year of the index` IS 2026, `month of the index` IS 3, `published on` IS YMD 2026 4 15, `value of the index` IS 100

GIVETH A LIST OF `Price index reading`
`the illustrative readings with one of April 2026` MEANS
    LIST `the reading published on 15 June 2025`
       , `the reading published on 15 July 2025`
       , `the reading published on 15 November 2025`
       , `the reading published on 15 April 2026`
       , `the reading published on 15 November 2026`

GIVETH AN `Inputs of regulation 3`
`inputs that take the amending regulations as these regulations` MEANS
    `Inputs of regulation 3` WITH
        `index readings` IS `the illustrative readings with one of April 2026`
        `the regulations came into force on` IS `the 2026 amendment of the Fees Regulations came into force on`
        `the reading of regulation 3` IS `the reading of regulation 3 that the encoding takes`
        `notices of the Director General` IS EMPTY

#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vA `for the service` sTheory `on the day` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, under` (`inputs that take the amending regulations as these regulations`) EQUALS JUST 162
#ASSERT `the fee payable in` vA `for the service` sTheory `on the day` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, under` (taken (`the illustrative readings with one of April 2026`)) EQUALS JUST 160

