§§ `The text as made, regulation 2(b): does "the exam" reach the theoretical exam?`

-- Taken: no, the one exam the regulations define is the practical exam.  Alternative: any exam, so an objection to a
-- theoretical score costs the same 40.
GIVEN x IS A MAYBE `Fee stated in a vintage`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount in the stated fee` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (f's `the amount stated`)

#ASSERT `the amount in the stated fee` (`the Fees Regulations as made state, reading "the exam" in regulation 2(b) as` `the exam is the one exam the regulations define` `, for the service` sObjTheory) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the amount in the stated fee` (`the Fees Regulations as made state, reading "the exam" in regulation 2(b) as` `the exam is any exam` `, for the service` sObjTheory) EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `the amount in the stated fee` (`the Fees Regulations as made state, reading "the exam" in regulation 2(b) as` `the exam is any exam` `, for the service` sObjPractical) EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `the amount in the stated fee` (`the Fees Regulations as made state, reading "the exam" in regulation 2(b) as` `the exam is any exam` `, for the service` sTheory) EQUALS NOTHING
